Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1356c8599c9dc6e4342904cc0cd0a087","RawContent":"&lt;div style=\"margin:20px; margin-top:5px; \"&gt; &lt;div class=\"smallfont\"&gt;Quote:&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\"&gt;  Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;affiwin&lt;\/strong&gt; &lt;img class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"&gt;  &lt;div style=\"font-style:italic\"&gt;You ladies are brave. I am such a control freak. I want to see and try dresses and know exactly what I&#039;m getting. I admire you all.&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/td&gt; &lt;\/tr&gt; &lt;\/table&gt; &lt;\/div&gt;LOL! \n \n I tried on dresses very similar to what I wanted, and if when they looked good I decided to order the dress online - in part because I couldn&#039;t find EXCATLY what I wanted in stores, and in part because it was a price too good to beat. \n \n If you love a certain style or even a certain dress, see if you can&#039;t find it online. And as long as its a close fit, you can always get it altered if its not perfect. Still might be cheaper than buying a dress from a salon that you will have to alter anyway.","Attachments":[],"Id":902017,"PostDate":1256744520,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <div  style=\"margin:20px\"> <div class=\"smallfont\">Quote:<\/div> <table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"> <tr> <td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\">  Originally Posted by <strong>affiwin<\/strong> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"><\/span>  <div  style=\"font-style:italic\">You ladies are brave. I am such a control freak. I want to see and try dresses and know exactly what I'm getting. I admire you all.<\/div> <\/td> <\/tr> <\/table> <\/div>LOL! <br \/> <br \/> I tried on dresses very similar to what I wanted, and if when they looked good I decided to order the dress online - in part because I couldn't find EXCATLY what I wanted in stores, and in part because it was a price too good to beat. <br \/> <br \/> If you love a certain style or even a certain dress, see if you can't find it online. And as long as its a close fit, you can always get it altered if its not perfect. Still might be cheaper than buying a dress from a salon that you will have to alter anyway.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><strong>21 people + Bride & Groom booked!!<\/strong><br><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;80\/st\/20100414\/e\/Beth+and+Jon%27s+Wedding%21\/dt\/1\/k\/8e20\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...8e20\/event.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"bholthof@connect.carleton.ca","IpAddress":"","GroupId":5,"GroupName":"Banned","JoinDate":1247538305,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-219399.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bholthof","Id":219399,"Name":"bholthof","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8d7e30b5160098ecad3101a869e89a73","RawContent":"&lt;div style=\"margin:20px; margin-top:5px; \"&gt; &lt;div class=\"smallfont\"&gt;Quote:&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\"&gt;  Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;affiwin&lt;\/strong&gt; &lt;img class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"&gt;  &lt;div style=\"font-style:italic\"&gt;You ladies are brave. I am such a control freak. I want to see and try dresses and know exactly what I&#039;m getting. I admire you all.&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/td&gt; &lt;\/tr&gt; &lt;\/table&gt; &lt;\/div&gt;I wouldn&#039;t really say that&#039;s true. I tried the original on in a store and knew it&#039;s what I wanted - just not what I could afford. Then the place I&#039;m ordering from will send me proof picts and I have the option not to buy it. So, I know before really committing if it&#039;s going to be close enough to make me happy. A lot of ladies CAN order a dress they haven&#039;t tried on or have a completely custom one made and be really happy. From past experiences I know this doesn&#039;t work out for me. I bought two sample wedding dresses on ebay and hadn&#039;t tried on either one. I got them and just wasn&#039;t in love with them. I also ordered my reception dress online (Amazon) and just got it yesterday. I was again, disappointed in the quality mostly. But that&#039;s really my fault for not asking the seller what the material was (they didn&#039;t list it). In this situation, I know I LOVE the style and know what kind of material they&#039;ll use so I have no reservations about it. \n \n But i&#039;m sure if you found something you liked in a store and knew the style\/fit were right for you - there&#039;d be no problem with the knockoff. As long as you ask the right questions and make sure the seller understands what you want, you can&#039;t go wrong!","Attachments":[],"Id":902064,"PostDate":1256745613,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <div  style=\"margin:20px\"> <div class=\"smallfont\">Quote:<\/div> <table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"> <tr> <td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\">  Originally Posted by <strong>affiwin<\/strong> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"><\/span>  <div  style=\"font-style:italic\">You ladies are brave. I am such a control freak. I want to see and try dresses and know exactly what I'm getting. I admire you all.<\/div> <\/td> <\/tr> <\/table> <\/div>I wouldn't really say that's true. I tried the original on in a store and knew it's what I wanted - just not what I could afford. Then the place I'm ordering from will send me proof picts and I have the option not to buy it. So, I know before really committing if it's going to be close enough to make me happy. A lot of ladies CAN order a dress they haven't tried on or have a completely custom one made and be really happy. From past experiences I know this doesn't work out for me. I bought two sample wedding dresses on ebay and hadn't tried on either one. I got them and just wasn't in love with them. I also ordered my reception dress online (Amazon) and just got it yesterday. I was again, disappointed in the quality mostly. But that's really my fault for not asking the seller what the material was (they didn't list it). In this situation, I know I LOVE the style and know what kind of material they'll use so I have no reservations about it. <br \/> <br \/> But i'm sure if you found something you liked in a store and knew the style\/fit were right for you - there'd be no problem with the knockoff. As long as you ask the right questions and make sure the seller understands what you want, you can't go wrong!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10748;0\/st\/20100223\/e\/Our+Wedding\/dt\/-2\/k\/67d5\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...67d5\/event.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"katie.torley@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1232061403,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-213991.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":67,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"KJT1985","Id":213991,"Name":"KJT1985","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3806651a9ae2db03bb52f91550f627d7","RawContent":"&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/s661.photobucket.com\/albums\/uu336\/raychelrae_photos\/Chiffon%20Wedding%20Gown\/\"&gt;Chiffon Wedding Gown pictures by raychelrae_photos - Photobucket&lt;\/a&gt;\n \n Ok, here was my shot at getting a knock-off. I finally got it and it is a beautiful dress! It&#039;s even very well made! I just do not like how it looks on my body type. I ordered it thinking it could be a TTD if anything. Not a bad dress, just not for me. SOOOO if anyone likes it I have a post in the &amp;quot;Sell, Trade, Freebie&amp;quot; category with this on there","Attachments":[],"Id":902746,"PostDate":1256761579,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <a href='http:\/\/s661.photobucket.com\/albums\/uu336\/raychelrae_photos\/Chiffon%20Wedding%20Gown\/' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Chiffon Wedding Gown pictures by raychelrae_photos - Photobucket<\/a><br \/> <br \/> Ok, here was my shot at getting a knock-off. I finally got it and it is a beautiful dress! It's even very well made! I just do not like how it looks on my body type. I ordered it thinking it could be a TTD if anything. Not a bad dress, just not for me. SOOOO if anyone likes it I have a post in the \"Sell, Trade, Freebie\" category with this on there\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/s3.amazonaws.com\/wedding_prod\/photos\/902409730c42f3a4f10b8d267a70454f_s\">http:\/\/s3.amazonaws.com\/wedding_prod...8d267a70454f_s<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"raychelrae@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1253395414,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-221802.gif?_